{"term":"tomb","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:2044dbcc2fadee862b","definition":"A small building, or a room within one, for the remains of the dead, with walls, a roof, and (if it is to be used for more than one corpse) a door. It may be partly or wholly in the ground (except for its entrance) in a cemetery, or it may be inside a church proper or in its crypt. Single tombs may be permanently sealed; those for families (or other groups) have doors for access whenever needed.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["burial chamber","sepulchre","vault"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["altar tomb","beehive tomb","chamber tomb","disentomb","empty as the tomb on Easter","entomb","the womb to the tomb","womb to tomb","passage tomb","Severn-Cotswold tomb","silent as the tomb","tombal","tomb bat","tombful","tombic","tombless","tomblet","tomblike","tombmate","tombology","tomb raider","tomb robber","tombstone","untomb","wedge tomb"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tomb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:94dd5d2fa7a114f44b","definition":"A pit in which the dead body of a human being is deposited.","example":"As one dead in the bottom of a tomb.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["grave"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly","register":"broadly","wordFamily":["altar tomb","beehive tomb","chamber tomb","disentomb","empty as the tomb on Easter","entomb","the womb to the tomb","womb to tomb","passage tomb","Severn-Cotswold tomb","silent as the tomb","tombal","tomb bat","tombful","tombic","tombless","tomblet","tomblike","tombmate","tombology","tomb raider","tomb robber","tombstone","untomb","wedge tomb"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tomb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:552f1d7716b7a0d260","definition":"One w